{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c497","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae75-a6d1-7e71-949a-c0aa2731b1b5"},"sequence":166,"recorded_at":1780531400000327,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"37dc71c1-9569-4ea8-89d7-d279257fe1a3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"37dc71c1-9569-4ea8-89d7-d279257fe1a3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"37dc71c1-9569-4ea8-89d7-d279257fe1a3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae77-314c-7d13-bbf9-e22c8dd6c22b"},"task_id":"01a0ae77-314c-7d13-bbf9-e22c8dd6c22b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae77-314c-7d13-bbf9-e22c8dd6c22b","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/base-refresh/replay-2355938507/worktree/LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-17\n7|\n8|<<<<<<< HEAD\n9|### TASK-260917-3lt2xv — release-agnostic cataloggen check via -adopted\n10|- CONTRACT: validation command 21 was pinned to explicit v0.6.0 inputs, so a Story re-pointing the catalog at a new revision failed construction at its own gate. The fix declares the adopted release once (`catalog.Adopted`, consumed by `Current()`) and adds a cataloggen `-adopted` mode deriving `internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json` and `internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json` relative to `-root` (default \".\"). Mixed `-adopted` with explicit `-metadata`/`-contracts`, a missing derived input (message names the derived path), and a lock whose source release differs from adopted are refused before generation; otherwise the same Generate call and `-check`/`-output` semantics run byte-identically to the explicit form.\n11|- GATE: command 21 is now `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; every other validation command unchanged. No catalog content, metadata, lock, or generated-output change.\n12|- TESTS: adopted positives, byte-identity (adopted vs explicit v0.6.0 vs committed), and all refusals driven through the production `run` entry; the configured-command test asserts the `-adopted` shape and runs it rooted at the repo. Narrowing mutants per refusal plus a byte-identity derivation mutant, all killed; harmless control SURVIVED. Both the candidate `-adopted` command and trunk's explicit command are green on the tree.\n13|- DOCS: README regenerate block and tool row document the `-adopted` form and the explicit equivalent. No behavior or availability claims added.\n14|=======\n15|### TASK-260830-2f5393 — implement Lease Record validation and CAS lifecycle\n16|- SCOPE (`internal/sessrepo/lease_store.go`): epoch-1 `create` leases from\n17|  the durable bootstrap inputs, successor leases through compare-and-swap,\n18|  fencing-token renewal, the operational grant-expiry policy, epoch\n19|  monotonicity (head plus one, never from input), host-UUIDv7 holder\n20|  identity, and tuple-ordered reads over content-addressed blobs with no\n21|  lease index to skew. Sections 2.2, 5.3, 13.6-13.10 (v0.6.0).\n22|- DESIGN: no second lease model — closed shape/identity stay with\n23|  `canonicaljson`, the tuple rule stays with `sessstate.Compare`\n24|  (restated as `CompareLeaseTuple` across the import cycle, pinned by a\n25|  cross-package agreement test), and `sessquery.winningLeaseFor` is\n26|  unchanged (an adoption test proves store-minted records admit there).\n27|  Mint failures are plain operational errors, never refusals, so a\n28|  weakened grammar gate fails closed at mint with a changed class —\n29|  which is what kills its narrowing mutant.\n30|- EXPIRY POLICY: the lease itself never expires (Section 5.3; pinned by\n31|  an ancient-`created_at` test); only the process-local fencing grant\n32|  lapses past the configured refresh interval, and revalidation renews\n33|  it. Grants are never persisted or replicated.\n34|- CAS IDEMPOTENCY: a retry names its pre-commit basis, so the replay\n35|  check re-mints against that basis (not the head) and answers the\n36|  persisted successor; this fixed a real bug found by the idempotency\n37|  test where head-minted retries minted epoch+2 and tripped token reuse.\n38|- CRASH: injector arms (`safe_retry` pre-write, `recoverable_parked`\n39|  post-commit with replay) plus real SIGKILL child drills at the\n40|  stage-then-rename seam for create and CAS, with fresh-handle reopen,\n41|  orphaned-temp tolerance, and exact-epoch retry assertions.\n42|- MUTANTS: the shipped `internal/sessrepo/testdata/mutate.py` battery\n43|  reports 27/27 applied plants killed (26 narrowing — one per new\n44|  `refuse` site — plus 1 token-preserving timestamp mutant); the\n45|  harmless control is `SURVIVED`,\n46|  `NOT_APPLIED`/`COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE` stay separate. The refusal\n47|  census grows to 61 sites (26 lease) and the equality census to three\n48|  ledgered sites.\n49|- COVERAGE: 8 of 8 shared-library AC rows driven by named production\n50|  entries; public CLI coverage is 0 of 8 by stated ownership bound.\n51|  Candidate left uncommitted in the managed Story worktree for handoff.\n52|>>>>>>> 0ebb7fa (TASK-260830-2f5393: TASK-260830-2f5393: implement-lease-record-validation-and-cas)\n53|\n54|### TASK-260830-21gygk — rev16 rework: normalize Go aliases in the sealed-capability census\n55|- REVIEW FINDING CLOSED (CR15 P2-A): the package-wide `go/types` census\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
