{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c7c3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae75-a6d1-7e71-949a-c0aa2731b1b5"},"sequence":572,"recorded_at":1780531400001139,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"37dc71c1-9569-4ea8-89d7-d279257fe1a3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"37dc71c1-9569-4ea8-89d7-d279257fe1a3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"37dc71c1-9569-4ea8-89d7-d279257fe1a3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae79-5b42-7c93-afb8-4c96f28b4415"},"task_id":"01a0ae79-5b42-7c93-afb8-4c96f28b4415","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae79-5b42-7c93-afb8-4c96f28b4415","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-22-1\",\n  \"command\": \"python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport subprocess\\nhead = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\",\\\"show\\\",\\\"HEAD:README.md\\\"],capture_output=True).stdout\\n# trunk regenerate block (exact)\\ntrunk_block = b\\\"\\\"\\\"```bash\\ngo generate ./internal/catalog\\ngo run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\ngo test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -count=1\\n```\\n\\nThe `-adopted` form derives the metadata and lock inputs from the code-level\\nadopted release, so the check stays valid when the adopted release changes.\\nThe explicit equivalent pins the same inputs by path:\\n\\n```bash\\ngo run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\n```\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nassert head.count(trunk_block)==1, \\\"trunk block not unique in HEAD\\\"\\np = \\\"README.md\\\"\\nsrc = open(p,\\\"rb\\\").read()\\nstale_block = b\\\"\\\"\\\"```bash\\ngo generate ./internal/catalog\\ngo run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\ngo test ./internal/catalog ./internal/cataloggen ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -count=1\\n```\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nassert src.count(stale_block)==1, \\\"stale block not unique in worktree\\\"\\nsrc = src.replace(stale_block, trunk_block)\\n# Go toolchain row: restore -adopted cell\\nold_cell = b\\\"`go generate ./internal/catalog`; `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -metadata internal/catalog/catalog.v0.6.0.json -contracts internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; `go test ./... -v`\\\"\\nnew_cell = b\\\"`go generate ./internal/catalog`; `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` (`-metadata`/`-contracts` select the same inputs explicitly); `go test ./... -v`\\\"\\nassert src.count(old_cell)==1, \\\"toolchain cell not unique\\\"\\nassert head.count(new_cell)==1, \\\"new cell not in HEAD\\\"\\nsrc = src.replace(old_cell, new_cell)\\nopen(p,\\\"wb\\\").write(src)\\nprint(\\\"README reconciled\\\")\\nEOF\\ngit diff --stat -- README.md; git diff -- README.md | grep -c '^-[^-]'; echo \\\"(removed-line count above; expect 1 for the 110->113 row)\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Restore trunk adopted text in README\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"README reconciled\\n README.md | 65 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-\\n 1 file changed, 64 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)\\n1\\n(removed-line count above; expect 1 for the 110->113 row)\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 207,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 52,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
