{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ccd3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae75-a6d1-7e71-949a-c0aa2731b1b5"},"sequence":1220,"recorded_at":1780531400002435,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"37dc71c1-9569-4ea8-89d7-d279257fe1a3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"37dc71c1-9569-4ea8-89d7-d279257fe1a3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"37dc71c1-9569-4ea8-89d7-d279257fe1a3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae8c-0537-7f21-ab1b-2916e08f9a53"},"task_id":"01a0ae8c-0537-7f21-ab1b-2916e08f9a53","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae8c-0537-7f21-ab1b-2916e08f9a53","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2atgj4/TASK-260830-2atgj4_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2atgj4 results: property-test the ownership reducer (final leaf)\n2|\n3|Role: developer. Worktree: `.temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree` on\n4|`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1oqfec`, candidate left UNCOMMITTED\n5|for the handoff snapshot. Status at handoff: ready for review.\n6|\n7|## Outcome\n8|\n9|The four story-pinned ownership invariants hold as 11 executable\n10|property tests over the landed production reducers\n11|(`sessstate.Reduce`/`Compare`, `sessrepo.WinningLease`/`ListLeases`,\n12|`fencing.Authorize*`), with hand-written closed-alphabet generators\n13|(no new module dependency), exhaustive enumeration where the space is\n14|small, and bounded seeded-random exploration otherwise. The\n15|union-order property exposed one genuine defect on the landed\n16|reducer and fixed it minimally with a RED-first regression (below).\n17|The falsification battery kills 8 narrowing plants through the named\n18|properties with an applied harmless SURVIVED control. Story-close\n19|items are carried: three traceability acceptance cases bound to the\n20|real reducers with honest coverage text and a re-pinned registry\n21|digest, the section:17.2 gap reword, the 3g12yp P3 vector, README and\n22|LOGBOOK updates, and the full configured validation suite green.\n23|\n24|## AC coverage: 18 of 18 rows driven, 0 stated bounds on behavior\n25|\n26|Every row is driven through the production entry point by a named\n27|committed test. Crash/idempotency: the changed derivation\n28|(`resolveWinner`) is pure with no durable mutation, so no new crash\n29|window exists; the landed lease crash/idempotency tests remain green\n30|(batch A). No unsupported capability is advertised (claims gate\n31|green; README adds no `ax`, `doctor`, or runtime claim).\n32|\n33|| # | AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) |\n34|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n35|| 1 | Union permutations project byte-identically | `sessstate.Reduce` | `TestOwnershipUnionOrderIndependent`, `TestOwnershipUnionOrderRegression` |\n36|| 2 | Successive-union partitions project byte-identically | `sessstate.Reduce` | `TestOwnershipUnionPartitionStable` |\n37|| 3 | Stale (lower-epoch) loser never dropped/rewritten/promoted | `sessstate.Reduce`; `sessrepo.GetLease`, `ListLeases` | `TestOwnershipLoserHistoryPreserved`, `TestOwnershipStoreLoserBytesPreserved` |\n38|| 4 | Same-epoch loser never dropped/rewritten/promoted, tie named | `sessstate.Reduce` | `TestOwnershipLoserHistoryPreserved` |\n39|| 5 | Winner is the greatest tuple; `Compare` is the total order | `sessstate.Compare` | `TestOwnershipWinnerIsTupleMaximum` |\n40|| 6 | `created_at` never influences store authority or fencing verdicts | `sessrepo.CreateLease`, `CompareAndSwapLease`, `WinningLease`, `VerifyFencingToken` | `TestOwnershipStoreClockNonAuthority` |\n41|| 7 | Absolute wall-clock position never influences gate verdicts | `fencing.Authorize*` (all five entries) | `TestOwnershipGateClockNonAuthority` |\n42|| 8 | At most one authoritative lease per session and epoch | `sessrepo.WinningLease`, `ListLeases`, `CompareAndSwapLease`, `GetLease` | `TestOwnershipStoreSingleAuthorityPerEpoch` |\n43|| 9 | Gates admit exactly the winner; pairwise exclusion | `fencing.Authorize*` (all five entries) | `TestOwnershipGateSingleAuthorizedOwner` |\n44|| 10 | Two handles/processes share one head; lagging CAS refuses stale | `sessrepo.CompareAndSwapLease`, `WinningLease` | `TestOwnershipStoreTwoHandlesOneHead` |\n45|| 11 | Exact contract fixtures pass | All entries above | Full suite green (batches A/B/C, 27 packages) |\n46|| 12 | Negative/refusal cases pass | All gates above | Full suite green; landed negatives untouched and green |\n47|| 13 | Crash/idempotency evidence where durable state mutates | (no new durable mutation) | Landed `TestCrashBeforeLeaseWriteIsSafeRetry`, `TestCrashAfterLeaseCommitCountsAsCommitted`, idempotent-retry tests green |\n48|| 14 | No unsupported capability advertised | README scan posture | `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim` et al. green |\n49|| 15 | P3 vector: epoch-zero third lease refuses `invalid_arguments` | `fencing.Authorize*` (all five entries) | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMalformedPresented/epoch_zero_other_lease` |\n50|| 16 | section:17.2 gap reworded to the narrower reader-enum meaning | `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json` | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` exit 0 |\n51|| 17 | Traceability cases bound with honest coverage, digest re-pinned | Registry + `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` | `TestVerifyRepositoryAcceptsExactOwnership` (113 cases), tracecheck pins |\n52|| 18 | Every property falsified by a narrowing mutant with controls | `internal/sessstate/testdata/mutate_properties.py` | 8 KILLED by named properties; harmless SURVIVED; harness exit 0 |\n53|\n54|## Defect found by the property (RED-first)\n55|\n56|`resolveWinner` reported each losing union lease against the transient\n57|arrival-order winner: with union `{R@1, A@1}` on an empty chain, one\n58|arrival order records R's loss and the other drops it entirely, and\n59|multi-entry unions name different losers-to targets per order. The\n60|winner was always right; the divergent-history evidence was not a\n61|function of the multiset. Fix (`internal/sessstate/sessstate.go`\n62|only): select the greatest tuple in a first pass, then report every\n63|entry below it in ascending tuple order naming the final winner, with\n64|the off-chain flag recomputed from the final winner (proven\n65|equivalent to the tracked flag in all cases). RED: 4 of 5 property\n66|tests fail on the landed code (`red-ownership-properties.log`).\n67|GREEN: 5 of 5 pass after the fix (`green-ownership-properties.log`).\n68|All landed union assertions were order-free, so the only collateral\n69|was the refusal-census line pins (sessstate.go:924/927 to :929/:932).\n70|\n71|## Files changed (candidate, uncommitted)\n72|\n73|- `internal/sessstate/sessstate.go`: two-pass `resolveWinner` (the fix).\n74|- `internal/sessstate/ownership_properties_test.go` (new): P1/P2\n75|  properties (5 tests).\n76|- `internal/sessrepo/lease_properties_test.go` (new): P3/P4 store\n77|  properties (4 tests).\n78|- `internal/fencing/ownership_properties_test.go` (new): P3/P4 gate\n79|  properties (2 tests).\n80|- `internal/fencing/gate_test.go`: P3 vector\n81|  `epoch_zero_other_lease`.\n82|- `internal/sessstate/testdata/mutate_properties.py` (new): the\n83|  falsification battery.\n84|- `internal/sessstate/census_state_test.go`: census line re-pin.\n85|- `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json`,\n86|  `internal/traceability/traceability.go` (digest re-pin),\n87|  `internal/traceability/traceability_test.go` (113),\n88|  `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go` (113 x2):\n89|  registry story-close.\n90|- `README.md`: property-suite section, harness table row, 113 figure.\n91|- `LOGBOOK.md`: task entry.\n92|\n93|## Validation (all local, real exits, this tree)\n94|\n95|- `go vet ./...`: exit 0. `GOOS=windows go vet ./...`: exit 0.\n96|  `gofmt -l internal`: empty. `go build ./...`: exit 0.\n97|  `GOOS=windows go build ./...`: exit 0.\n98|