44|| 10 | Two handles/processes share one head; lagging CAS refuses stale | `sessrepo.CompareAndSwapLease`, `WinningLease` | `TestOwnershipStoreTwoHandlesOneHead` |\n45|| 11 | Exact contract fixtures pass | All entries above | Full suite green (batches A/B/C, 27 packages) |\n46|| 12 | Negative/refusal cases pass | All gates above | Full suite green; landed negatives untouched and green |\n47|| 13 | Crash/idempotency evidence where durable state mutates | (no new durable mutation) | Landed `TestCrashBeforeLeaseWriteIsSafeRetry`, `TestCrashAfterLeaseCommitCountsAsCommitted`, idempotent-retry tests green |\n48|| 14 | No unsupported capability advertised | README scan posture | `TestRealREADMECarriesNoPositiveClaim` et al. green |\n49|| 15 | P3 vector: epoch-zero third lease refuses `invalid_arguments` | `fencing.Authorize*` (all five entries) | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMalformedPresented/epoch_zero_other_lease` |\n50|| 16 | section:17.2 gap reworded to the narrower reader-enum meaning | `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json` | `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` exit 0 |\n51|| 17 | Traceability cases bound with honest coverage, digest re-pinned | Registry + `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` | `TestVerifyRepositoryAcceptsExactOwnership` (113 cases), tracecheck pins |\n52|| 18 | Every property falsified by a narrowing mutant with controls | `internal/sessstate/testdata/mutate_properties.py` | 8 KILLED by named properties; harmless SURVIVED; harness exit 0 |\n53|\n54|## Defect found by the property (RED-first)\n55|\n56|`resolveWinner` reported each losing union lease against the transient\n57|arrival-order winner: with union `{R@1, A@1}` on an empty chain, one\n58|arrival order records R's loss and the other drops it entirely, and\n59|multi-entry unions name different losers-to targets per order. The\n60|winner was always right; the divergent-history evidence was not a\n61|function of the multiset. Fix (`internal/sessstate/sessstate.go`\n62|only): select t